{
  "format": "SIDPULSE",
  "format_version": 6,
  "song": {
    "title": "Autumn at five",
    "author": "SIDpulse Tracker",
    "comments": "Autumn at five\nAn original welcome song for SIDpulse Tracker.\nA quiet walk through damp woods before sunrise. D minor, 80 BPM, 32 bars, 96 seconds.\nVoice 1: slow triangle melody, with spaces for its release.\nVoice 2: low triangle roots, held across each two-bar harmony.\nVoice 3: soft eighth-note arpeggios under one swelling envelope.\nThe SID has no dedicated sine oscillator: triangle and the shared low-pass give the rounded tone.\nNo samples, external effects or additional sound voices.\nF4 edits envelopes/arpeggio tables; F11 shows the named arrangement; F8 stops.\nThe ending releases into a short breath before the loop. All music is editable here.",
    "sid_model": "8580",
    "clock": "NTSC",
    "speed": 6,
    "tempo": 80,
